# Build before release

Before any **push**, **PR**, or **release** of app/code changes:

1. Run `ALLOW_LOCAL_STACK_ENV=1 npm run build` (local lacks hosted production env; this still runs compile + TypeScript like Vercel).
2. Fix failures before committing/pushing.
3. Do not push knowing the last build failed.

If only docs/scripts/tmp change with no app compile path, typecheck alone (`npx tsc --noEmit`) is enough — prefer full build when `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, or `types/` changed.
